# NOTICE

## Wallpaper files are not part of this project

This plugin **reads** wallpaper files that already exist on your machine, from a local
Wallpaper Engine installation. It does not bundle, host, mirror, or redistribute any
wallpaper.

Wallpapers from the Steam Workshop belong to their respective authors. They are included
in this repository in no form whatsoever — no `.mp4`, `.pkg`, `.tex`, preview image, or
Wallpaper Engine `project.json` is committed here, and `.gitignore` excludes the caches
that reference them.

The screenshots and fixtures referenced in the tests point at whatever library the
machine running the tests happens to have. They are not shipped.

## If you fork this

Do not add wallpaper content to your fork. Point the plugin at your own local library
instead, and respect each Workshop author's terms.

## Third-party runtime dependencies

The plugin itself has **no runtime dependencies**. It uses only the Node.js standard
library (`node:fs`, `node:http`, `node:crypto`, `node:path`, `node:os`,
`node:child_process`) and browser APIs.

The test scripts optionally use [Playwright](https://playwright.dev/) for the live
browser suites; it is not required to install or run the plugin.

